content.text:
Now bottom-center CSS polish and add debug API. Also ensure the ult label readable by changing HTML structure? Simpler CSS:
```
.bottom-center {bottom: 24px}
.ability {width: 84px}
.ability small {font-size:6.5px; letter-spacing:.6px}
.ultimate {width: 158px; padding:0 6px 8px 10px; gap:9px}
.ultimate strong {font:700 9.5px/9.5px var(--display); letter-spacing:.6px; white-space:nowrap}
.ult-charge {height:2px}
```
But "PRISMATIC<br/>BREACH" with nowrap means each line no wrap. Fine.

Also abilities `.ability .cooldown {bottom:19px; left:24px; width:35px}` depends widths. Center alignment: icon at center. `.cooldown` left should be 50% translate. Change to `left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%) scaleX(0)` but JS sets transform scaleX only which would kill translate. Instead wrap center via `left:calc(50% - 17.5px)`.

Current .cooldown bottom:15px height 2; icon 35 high, small label below. Fine.

Let's fix widths.

