Hmm the rim positioning is wrong (size/2 vs 0 combos). Let me instead simply add 4 edges at x=±size/2, z=±size/2 with proper orientation. Replace loop:

```
for (const sx of [-1,1]) for (const sz of [-1,1]) {
  const rimX = new Mesh(BoxGeometry(size, .035, .035), mat); rimX.position.set(0? ...)
}
```
Top rim rectangle edges: edge along X at z=±size/2, and edge along Z at x=±size/2.

```
for (const s of [-1,1]) {
 const ex = new Mesh(box(size, .035,.035), mat); ex.position.set(0, height-0.05, s*size/2); g.add(ex);
 const ez = new Mesh(box(.035,.035,size), mat); ez.position.set(s*size/2, height-0.05, 0); g.add(ez);
}
```
Do that.

