import { createRequire } from 'node:module';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const runtime = '/home/runner/.local/share/omgithub-playwright';
const require = createRequire(runtime + '/package.json');
const { chromium, devices } = require('playwright');
const cfg = JSON.parse(readFileSync(runtime + '/linux.json', 'utf8'));
process.env.DISPLAY ||= ':' + readFileSync(runtime + '/display', 'utf8').trim();
const browser = await chromium.launch({ ...cfg.browser.launchOptions, timeout: 40000 });
const ctx = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 390, height: 844 }, isMobile: true, hasTouch: true, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });
const page = await ctx.newPage();
const errs = [];
page.on('pageerror', e => errs.push(e.message));
await page.goto('http://127.0.0.1:3002/', { waitUntil: 'load', timeout: 45000 });
await page.waitForTimeout(1500);
await page.screenshot({ path: '/tmp/m1.jpg', type: 'jpeg', quality: 82 });
await page.tap('#start-btn');
await page.waitForTimeout(1800);
await page.screenshot({ path: '/tmp/m2.jpg', type: 'jpeg', quality: 82 });
const info = await page.evaluate(() => ({
  mode: window.__prism.phase.mode,
  touchVisible: getComputedStyle(document.getElementById('touch-controls')).display,
  banner: getComputedStyle(document.getElementById('round-banner')).display,
  touch: matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches,
  hud: document.getElementById('hud').className
}));
console.log(JSON.stringify({ info, errs }, null, 2));
await browser.close();

content.text:
Mobile gameplay has significant layout issues:
1. The touch reload button "R" appears at top-left overlapping the brand (because `.touch-reload` base? It's positioned right:99px bottom:212px, but in the screenshot there's an R at top-left at (14,63) and another "R" button at (14, ~63)? Wait the "R" top-left is likely the reload button with CSS not applying? There are two R? At top-left x 14,y 50-78 a vertical button with "R" — that's the touch-reload but positioned wrong? bottom:212px means 212 from bottom = y 632. Hmm top-left R is likely the `.touch-reload` with `position:absolute` inside `.touch-controls` which has inset 0 and pointer-events none; but CSS `.touch-reload{right:99px;bottom:212px;...}` should be bottom-right. Unless `.touch-reload` has no position rule because I defined it in the media only? Yes: `.touch-ult,.touch-reload{...}` in media with position? The media rule sets width/height/display but not `position:absolute`. The earlier combined rule `.touch-fire,.touch-jump,.touch-dash,.touch-scan{position:absolute;...}` doesn't include ult/reload. So they default to static → appear at top-left. Fix by adding position:absolute and styling to ult/reload. Same for border-radius/color base.

2. The minimap overlaps the mission strip at top-left (map top 103, mission strip top 66 height 27; fine) but its label is under mission. The toast "MISSION LIVE" at top 152 overlaps the minimap and extends to the right; it's positioned center at 152, overlapping. On mobile move toast to top 210 or below the minimap? It's centered; the minimap occupies left 12-125. Toast centered width ~200 at x 95-295 → overlaps. Move mobile toast to top 245 or use bottom. Better: show toasts at bottom center above the ability row (bottom 120). But that overlaps gameplay. Use top: 240px and full width? For mobile, set `.toast{top:245px; font-size:7px; max-width:70vw; text-align:center}`.

3. The bottom HUD overlaps heavily: health 100 at left and ammo 25 at right, ability row center all crammed at the very bottom, with weapon slots overlapping the ultimate labels. On mobile, the layout needs a cleaner arrangement:
   - Hide weapon slots on mobile (or make a compact single row above ammo).
   - Move ability row up (bottom: 100px) to avoid the ammo row? Actually thumb controls occupy bottom right; ability row at bottom center would be behind joystick/fire. Better: place abilities at the TOP-center below the mission strip? Hmm.

   Mobile FPS layout: joystick bottom-left, fire bottom-right, jump/dash/scan/ult above fire, health top-left under minimap? It's currently bottom-left overlapped by the joystick (joystick at left 20 bottom 100, health at left 13 bottom 20). The health row is at the bottom-left, below the joystick; the joystick is at y 632-744, health at y 770 — okay but the touch stick knob overlaps.

   The bottom center ability row is at bottom 17 (y 750-830) colliding with health/ammo and weapon slots. Since mobile already has touch ability buttons, hide the bottom-center ability row entirely on mobile. Hide the weapon slots too, or show only the current weapon + ammo at bottom-right. Hide `.weapon-slots` and `.bottom-center` on mobile. Move `.bottom-right` up to bottom 150? The fire button is at bottom 103 (y 672-741) and jump 112; bottom-right ammo at bottom 17 y 760-827, width 148 starting x 230; the fire button (right 21, w69) is at x 300-369 y 672; so ammo at y 760 is below fire, fine. But the weapon slots at y 800-824 (right) collide with the ammo text. Hide weapon slots.

   Health at left bottom 20 (y 770) with joystick above, fine—but the bar and player tag sit at the very bottom, okay. The screenshot shows health at y 775 with "PHASE RUNNER" below and the ability row overlapping it. Hiding bottom-center fixes.

   The minimap: at top-left 113px wide; okay. But mission strip spans 66-93 and the map from 103. Fine; the "MISSION LIVE" toast overlaps.

4. The touch-ult "Q" and scan "C" are at right, but ult is above scan (right 24 bottom 226 → y 585) and C at right 23 bottom 183 → y 626; fire at y 672. Jump at right 98 bottom 112 → y 689 (x 249-292). Dash at right 97 bottom 164 → y 637. So the vertical stack: ult (585), scan (626), dash (637), fire (672), jump (689). Overlaps between scan (C at x 332-367) and dash (x 255-293) not; ult at x 333. Fine.

5. The "R" at top-left is the bug. Fix.

6. The gameplay camera at spawn shows the enemy far left (a small orange robot) and a big black box (crate) center. Because the player spawns at (13,33) facing center; the black box in the middle is the crate at (8,20)? It's 2.5 wide, appears far, but the black mass center at y 460-530 is a crate. Fine.

7. The sky looks great on mobile.

8. The topbar: brand + timer + "18 MS" + "PAUSE" overlap. Hide ping/menu-chip and round-label/sub as planned.

9. The kill feed at top right could collide with toast; it's fine.

10. The mission strip is too wide and overlaps the minimap top? It ends at 375 width, starts 15; minimap at 103. Fine.

11. The ability "E" card at bottom center is behind the joystick; hide.

12. The gun is not visible at all on mobile (weapon rig visible but camera FOV? At 390 width the gun should show bottom right; the screenshot bottom right is covered by HUD and fire button). The gun might be there but hidden behind HUD; I see no gun. Wait, on mobile the aspect is tall; the viewmodel at x 0.36 is far right, possibly off-screen due to narrower horizontal FOV? With vertical FOV 74 and aspect 0.46, horizontal FOV is ~41°, so x 0.36 at z 0.74 → 26° horizontally, near the edge → visible but cut. I don't see it. The gun may be off-screen to the right or hidden below. This is bad for a shooter: need the gun visible on mobile.

   Fix: adjust weapon position based on aspect ratio: for narrow screens, use a separate layout with x 0.2, y -0.26, z -0.62 and scale 0.55. Or compute in guns: if camera.aspect < 0.8, use mobile base positions. Implement in update: choose base/ads variants based on camera.aspect. Simpler: create a scale factor: rig.position/scale? Set `rig.scale.setScalar(0.8)` and shift? The gun is a child of camera; changing rig position moves all. On mobile, set rig.position.set(-0.1, -0.02, 0.12) and scale .85 to bring the gun inward and slightly closer? gun group base x .36 is in rig coordinates; with aspect narrow it is at 26° which is close to the right edge (hFOV/2 ≈ 21°), so it's off-screen. Need x ≈ 0.22. 

   I'll add a `layout` factor in guns.update: if `camera.aspect < 0.9`, target positions adjusted: multiply x by 0.62 and z by 0.9, y +0.02. Since base is constant object, compute per-frame:
   ```
   const aspectScale = camera.aspect < 0.9 ? 0.6 : 1;
   b.group.position.x = lerp(bp.pos.x..., ) * aspectScale ...
   ```
   Careful with lerpVectors into position then multiply x. Simple: after lerpVectors and offsets, if narrow: position.x *= 0.58; position.y += 0.02. Also scale guns? The gun will appear larger relative to the narrow screen; maybe scale 0.85 to compensate. Set in createWeapons: `const aspect = camera.aspect; if (aspect<0.9) built.forEach(b=>b.group.scale.setScalar(0.6))` and positions x 0.2.

   Add a resize handler to update scale? Camera aspect changes on rotate; could update inside update() based on camera.aspect:
   ```
   const scale = camera.aspect < 0.9 ? 0.62 : 0.66;
   b.group.scale.setScalar(scale);
   ```
   And multiply x positions by (aspect<0.9 ? 0.55 : 1). Good.

13. The gun should show in the mobile screenshot; with this fix it will.

14. Touch aim: swiping on the right half is fine; but the whole screen except right half doesn't look. The right control buttons occupy the right half; swiping in empty areas works.

15. On mobile, the start overlay's HUD uses 0.18 opacity and is fine.

Also the top-left "R" bug fix.

Let me apply mobile CSS changes:
```
@media(max-width:700px){
 .ping,.menu-chip,.round-label,.round-sub{display:none}
 .brand b{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:1px}
 .brand small{display:none}
 .brand-mark{width:28px;height:28px}
 .round-info{top:12px}
 .round-timer{font-size:22px}
 .bottom-center{display:none}
 .weapon-slots{display:none}
 .toast{top:238px;font-size:7px;max-width:74vw;text-align:center;white-space:normal}
 .bottom-right{bottom:16px;width:140px}
 .bottom-left{bottom:16px}
 .health-row>b{font-size:22px}
 .player-tag{font-size:6px}
}
```
Also `.mission-strip` may overlap the minimap at top 66 and minimap top 103. Fine.

Hide the brand's small line; the brand mark and name remain.

Also the "R" button fix in base:
```
.touch-ult,.touch-reload{position:absolute;pointer-events:auto;touch-action:none;border-radius:50%;color:var(--teal);background:rgba(6,23,25,.6);border:1px solid rgba(104,246,220,.46);font:11px var(--mono)}
```
Then media sets positions.

Mobile ult button color orange.

Gun mobile layout.

Also mobile timer/health overlap? fine.

Apply.

