content.text:
Now the fire button is at (754,218) 69x69, but the landscape media should override it to (766,288) 58x58. Why is it (754,218)? Because the landscape media rule is *before* the new appended global rules, and both have specificity `body.is-touch .touch-fire` (0,2,1) — the later appended rule wins. Oops. The appending order: the existing end block had the landscape media; I appended the global rules after it. So the global fire position wins over the landscape override.

Need to move/duplicate the landscape override *after* the global rules, or use higher specificity / !important. Easiest: append a new landscape media block at the very end (after the global rules) with the fire/jump/dash/scan positions and stick. The previous landscape media is now partially overridden by the later global rules for stick? The global stick comes before the landscape media in the existing end block, so the media wins for the stick. For the newly appended global fire rules, they come after the landscape media → they win. Re-add the landscape override at the end.

Also the fire at (754,218) overlaps the jump (703,235) partially (fire x754-823 vs jump 703-746 → no). The ammo is centered, fine. But I want the landscape-specific positions. Append:

```
@media(orientation:landscape) and (max-height:540px){
 body.is-touch .touch-fire{right:20px;bottom:44px;width:58px;height:58px;font-size:24px}
 ...
}
```
appears after the globals. Same for jump/dash/scan. The ult/reload/weapon and stick rules from the earlier landscape media still apply (no later global equivalents except the new fire group). The `.touch-ult` global rules are before the earlier landscape media, so the media wins. Good.

Append the landscape overrides for fire/jump/dash/scan only (and maybe stick for safety).

